abstract: >-
  A self-contained Lean 4 (v4.36.0 / Mathlib v4.36.0) formalization establishing new
  machine-verified upper bounds on reset thresholds of synchronizing deterministic finite
  automata, including: (1) the first general asymptotic upper bound strictly below
  (7/48) n^3 and an explicit-O(n^2) bound (24646/149769) n^3 + 50 n^2 beating Shitov (2019);
  (2) the bound 2n^2 - 8n + 9 beating Zhu (FSTTCS 2024) on the full class of synchronizing
  automata with a transitive permutation group and defect-1 letters, together with an
  improved bound for completely reachable automata over Ferens and Szykula (2025) and
  zero-error congruence-collapse bounds; (3) exact (n-1)^2 and quadratic bounds beyond
  one-cluster automata (cluster-balanced, opposite-drift, cyclic-basin, partial-drain,
  non-strongly-connected 2-cycle, almost-uniform, two-value stationary, and super-Eulerian
  automata); and (4) complete formalizations of Zhu's July 2026 one-cluster theorem and
  classical landmarks (Cerny 1964, Frankl-Pin 1982/83, Eppstein 1990, Dubuc 1998, Kari 2003,
  and Shitov 2019). All proofs compile with zero sorry and depend only on standard Lean axioms.
